engths, impairment, environment, and accommodations"}, {"id": "03216caf-2518-45d4-9020-a5d82d4d4079", "type": "concept", "title": "Stigma and ethical language"}], "description": "Students learn respectful, evidence-based approaches to variation in brain and behavior."}]}, {"id": "07f8b551-0ef1-4a19-ac49-36aa4af069b5", "type": "topic", "title": "Neurological and Neurodegenerative Disorders, Injury, and Clinical Correlations", "description": "This module introduces brain disorders, localization, neural vulnerability, and rehabilitation-relevant concepts.", "children": [{"id": "e0ba2462-1077-478f-b285-fcbd431cb7a7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Localization and symptoms", "children": [{"id": "06e1666f-284e-487d-865a-3185cc4ecb69", "type": "concept", "title": "Stroke, traumatic brain injury, seizures, and tumors overview"}, {"id": "81535941-9dc1-4359-b8db-42e92e1aa0af", "type": "concept", "title": "Lesion logic and disconnection"}, {"id": "431dc5e0-5768-44d7-bed7-abf78f6e4681", "type": "concept", "title": "Neurological exam concepts"}], "description": "Clinical correlations show how brain systems support behavior."}, {"id": "69838721-6c56-4ed0-aaef-a6ab8e8d1dca", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Neurodegeneration", "children": [{"id": "1b5dab22-6ce2-4f65-89bb-cba35a2e7a42", "type": "concept", "title": "Alzheimer disease and dementias"}, {"id": "952f33d3-5aa3-4127-a475-9ebaff14d33c", "type": "concept", "title": "Parkinson disease and movement disorders"}, {"id": "8a3a20bc-dfc3-415b-bf9b-692d1756bd95", "type": "concept", "title": "Huntington disease, ALS, and demyelinating disease overview"}], "description": "Students learn major patterns of progressive neural vulnerability."}, {"id": "cac636a0-dd87-4690-8c58-9817cbb214dc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Recovery and care", "children": [{"id": "76c2f646-a09c-4a48-95ac-5ab2cfa18e06", "type": "concept", "title": "Neurorehabilitation principles"}, {"id": "9377e4a5-109f-4fa4-b597-022fd4e31dc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Compe